speechtext:
It reads:
The hoard and the chief commissioner shall have jurisdiction, upon or without complaint made, to inquire into any matter relating to
(a)	the grading of any grain;
(b)	the weighing of any grain;
(c)	the deductions made from any grain for storage or shrinkage;

It continues:
(f)	the deterioration of any grain during storage or treatment;
(g)	the refusal or neglect of any person to comply with any provision of the act;
(h)	any other matter arising out of the performance of the duties of the board.
